  "keywords": ["linux", "nvidia", "dgx-spark", "cluster", "qwen3.8", "flash-next", "nvfp4", "vllm", "mtp", "expert-parallel"],
  "capabilities": ["chat", "responses", "anthropic-messages", "streaming", "usage", "tools", "reasoning", "vision", "mtp", "moe", "long-context"],
  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "Two directly connected DGX Spark systems",
    "notes": [
      "TP=2 plus expert parallel runs over the private ConnectX-7 RoCE fabric and starts worker-first under LLooM. NCCL selects IPv4 RoCE-v2 independently on each Spark instead of assuming a shared GID-table index.",
      "The pinned vLLM image is the ARM64 manifest used by MiaAI commit 169fbad266f2791335a3102f0d3d625e7c295563. Its exact PLE source hash is guarded before enabling the checkpoint's existing FP8 PLE method.",
      "Native 262144-token context deliberately omits YaRN. The checkpoint's supported BF16 hybrid cache is retained; FP8 KV is not enabled without separate QSA/GDN correctness evidence.",
      "MiaAI measured 35.11 GiB of KV memory and 2,481,424 cache tokens at GPU memory utilization 0.835. At native context this is enough for roughly nine full-context sequences; LLooM keeps entity-shaped admission below that physical ceiling and owns the bounded overflow queue.",
      "A tight three-request stagger showed vLLM executing two requests while holding the third internally. LLooM therefore admits two entity requests and owns overflow queueing rather than duplicating the backend's opaque wait queue.",
      "The full-pair lane displaces resident Spark GPU sidecars while active. Alias-member suspension keeps production q38fn traffic on external members during recipe work and prevents background admission from fighting controlled benchmarks."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": {
